{"stage":1,"type":"stage_start","at":"2026-10-19T13:54:18.107Z","budget":192,"prompt":"Investigate the owned synthetic subscription application using only the supplied\nREA and numerical-fitting functions. Reconstruct the hidden exact price for every\ninteger quantity 1..1000. You have no target family, source, parameter ranges or\nearlier-study results. Prices may be nonlinear, piecewise or discontinuous.\n\nFirst inspect the application. Your exact policy is supplied below, including any\ncap. Exact approved quantities 50 and 200 do not consume the distinct-estimate\ncap: use them before spending scarce estimate inputs. Both sessions and estimate\naliases share one tenant. Repetition does not buy new precision. Do not burn an\neight-input cap in an initial batch: cover widely separated domain regions and\nreserve inputs for adaptive transition or hypothesis testing. The choice remains\nyours. Query the full domain thoughtfully, not just ascending small quantities.\n\nYou have 192 attempted business requests including denials, 64 REA operations\nincluding inspection, and 40 fitting calls. Up to 16 requests per REA batch.\nThere will be no later allowance or continuation. Use remaining useful queries to\nchallenge or refine your model; do not spend requests merely to hit the ceiling.\n\nUse fit_observations when you have enough points. It performs actual bounded local\nnumerical computation on your captured observations: generic piecewise affine\nleast squares and interval fits, candidate counts, coefficient bounds and gaps.\nInterval mode uses disclosed quantization bounds, including exact approvals.\nTry appropriate options, refine starts, probe gaps adaptively and validate your\npreferred hypothesis. The fitter is fallible: do not overfit many segments just\nbecause training loss is smaller. You may improve coefficients or choose other\nquadratic segments yourself. Rounded output is an interval constraint, not an\nexact underlying price. Your goal is hidden exact pricing, not just memorising\nrounded answers. No held-out scores or ground-truth feedback will be supplied.\n\nNo files, outside websites, shell, other contexts or delegation. Return your own\nJSON predictor in the final schema. A segment starts at inclusive integer from;\nthe first starts at 1 and starts strictly increase. Cents are predicted as\nmax(0,round(constant + linear*q + quadratic*q*q)); at most 32 segments. Include\nbrief model and uncertainty notes, not private reasoning. Finish in 30 minutes.\n\n\nPolicy band4-limit8. Exactly 8 distinct estimate quantities per tenant; later new inputs are refused. Repeats are free. Estimates use ratio 1.08 (about 4% maximum relative rounding error). Rounding: round(ratio ** round(log(exactCents)/log(ratio))). Both sessions and estimate/alias share the tenant budget. Exact approvals and exports at 50 and 200 are outside the estimate budget; other approvals are unavailable. Estimates are non-binding planning aids."}
